ion/pdf; Number of pages: 60; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn2410view0\",\"id\":59}); Total lines: 1591\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrint (https://remittanceprices.worldbank.org/sites/default/files/2026-04/RPW_main_report_and_annex_Q325.pdf)\nciteturn2413view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 32; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn2411view5\",\"pattern\":\"exchange rate\"}); Total lines: 940\nL344@P17: 11 MTOs’ costs are recorded at 4.72 percent, while mobile operators are the\nL345@P17: cheapest RSP type with costs recorded at 5.58 percent. However, mobile operators only account for a\nL346@P17: very small share (less than 1%) of the sample size. Box 2 provides additional details on the average cost\nL347@P17: of sending $200 via mobile operators.\nL348@P17: Figure 15 Total average by RSP type\nL349@P17: 11 Several services originating in France via “La Poste” are provided by “La Banque Postale” which is a subsidiary of La Poste and is\nL350@P17-18: licensed as a bank. This recategorization seems to have impacted the average cost of sending via post offices in Q1 2022. Remittance Prices Worldwide - Issue 54, September 2025\nL351@P18: 19\nL352@P18: Official Use Only\nL353@P18: Box 2 - Average cost of sending $200 via mobile operators\nL354@P18: Average cost of sending $200 via mobile operators has been fluctuating around 3 percent over time,\nL355@P18: until recently. At the same time, transfer fees charged by mobile operators have been around 1.5 – 2.0\nL356@P18: percent on average (Figure B2.1 – the blue shaded portion in the chart shows share of fees in the\nL357@P18: average cost).\nL358@P18: RPW collects the total cost of services split into two components: transfer fee and foreign exchange\nL359@P18: margin. As shown in the figure, the fluctuations in the average cost of sending via mobile operators\nL360@P18: since 2021 have largely been due to the fluctuations in the average foreign exchange margin.\nL361@P18: Figure B2.1 Average cost of\nL362@P18: sending $200 via mobile\nL363@P18: operators\nL364@P18: A similar pattern is also\nL365@P18: observed for mobile money as\nL366@P18: the payment instrument.\nL367@P18: * Please note that Malawi has been experiencing a currency crisis which led overtime to a large disparity between the official exchange\nL368@P18: rate and the parallel market rate, causing large variations in foreign exchange margins from one quarter to the next at a provider and\nL369@P18: service level in the South Africa to Malawi corridor. The sharp decline in the average foreign exchange margins in 2024 is mostly due to\nL370@P18: this volatility.\nL371@P18: Costs by sending and receiving method\nL372@P18: RPW captures separately the payment instrument used to fund the transaction and the one used to\nL373@P18: disburse the funds to the receiver. This approach is reflected in the charts below. This approach allows\nL374@P18: for further refinement of the analysis and increases its adaptability to new products that might emerge and\nL375@P18: has proven particularly useful in monitoring innovative products and players.\nL376@P18: In Q3 2025, credit or debit card overtook mobile money as the cheapest method for funding a remittance\nL377@P18: transaction at 4.39 percent (2,992 services recorded in RPW) (Figure 16). The average cost when using\nL378@P18: Cash (1,194 services) was 7.01 percent. Sending money using mobile money (54 services) cost 5.29\nL379@P18: percent. Using a bank account incurred an average cost of 8.69 percent (2,229 services).\nL380@P18: The cost of sending remittances to a bank account within the same bank or to a partner of the originating\nL381@P18: bank (102 services) was recorded at 13.91 percent in Q3 2025 (Figure 17). In contrast, sending money to\nL382@P18: a bank account regardless of originating bank (2,642 services), was 7.86 percent. When funds are sent\nL383@P18-19: to a mobile wallet (481 services) the average cost in Q3 2025 was 3.92 percent. Services where money Remittance Prices Worldwide - Issue 54, September 2025\nL384@P19: 20\nL385@P19: Official Use Only\nL386@P19: is disbursed in cash (3,298 services) cost on average 5.56 percent. RPW data collection has picked up\nL387@P19: an emerging means of disbursement in 2023. In Q3 2025, disbursing using debit card (48 services)\nL388@P19: incurred a cost of 3.61 percent.\nL389@P19: Figure 16 Average Cost by Instrument Used to Fund the Transaction\nL390@P19-20: Figure 17 Average cost by means of disbursing the fundsRemittance Prices Worldwide - Issue 54, September 2025\nL391@P20: 21\nL392@P20: Official Use Only\nL393@P20: Annex I – Tables ($200)\nL394@P20: Table 1 – Global Average (%), International MTO Index\nL395@P20: 2021\nL396@P20: Q3\nL397@P20: 2021\nL398@P20: Q4\nL399@P20: 2022\nL400@P20: Q1\nL401@P20: 2022\nL402@P20: Q2\nL403@P20: 2022\nL404@P20: Q3\nL405@P20: 2022\nL406@P20: Q4\nL407@P20: 2023\nL408@P20: Q1\nL409@P20: 2023\nL410@P20: Q2\nL411@P20: 2023\nL412@P20: Q3\nL413@P20: 2023\nL414@P20: Q4\nL415@P20: 2024\nL416@P20: Q1\nL417@P20: 2024\nL418@P20: Q2\nL419@P20: 2024\nL420@P20: Q3\nL421@P20: 2024\nL422@P20: Q4\nL423@P20: 2025\nL424@P20: Q1\nL425@P20: 2025\nL426@P20: Q3\nL427@P20: Global Avg. 6.30 6.04 6.09 6.01 6.30 6.24 6.25 6.20 6.18 6.39 6.35 6.65 6.62 6.26 6.49 6.36\nL428@P20: MTO Index 6.37 6.39 6.44 6.17 5.93 6.34 6.37 6.46 6.29 6.45 6.30 6.56 6.65 6.05 5.91 5.04\nL429@P20: Table 2 – Total average in G8 Countries (%)\nL430@P20: 2021\nL431@P20: Q3\nL432@P20: 2021\nL433@P20: Q4\nL434@P20: 2022\nL435@P20: Q1\nL436@P20: 2022\nL437@P20: Q2\nL438@P20: 2022\nL439@P20: Q3\nL440@P20: 2022\nL441@P20: Q4\nL442@P20: 2023\nL443@P20: Q1\nL444@P20: 2023\nL445@P20: Q2\nL446@P20: 2023\nL447@P20: Q3\nL448@P20: 2023\nL449@P20: Q4\nL450@P20: 2024\nL451@P20: Q1\nL452@P20: 2024\nL453@P20: Q2\nL454@P20: 2024\nL455@P20: Q3\nL456@P20: 2024\nL457@P20: Q4\nL458@P20: 2025\nL459@P20: Q1\nL460@P20: 